---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How ExoSquare handles information when you visit this website or contact us."
  ><div class="wrap legal-page">
    <header class="page-header">
      <div class="eyebrow">ExoSquare</div><h1>Privacy policy</h1><p>
        How ExoSquare handles information when you visit this website or contact
        us.
      </p><p class="legal-date">Last updated 7 September 2026</p>
    </header><section class="editorial-grid contact-section">
      <h2>About this policy</h2><div class="prose">
        <p>
          This policy explains how ExoSquare handles personal information in
          connection with this website and enquiries about our work.
        </p><p>
          “ExoSquare”, “we”, “us” and “our” refer collectively to Exosquare
          Limited in Hong Kong (business registration number 75803217) and
          Exosquare Pty. Ltd. in Australia (ACN 621 091 254). For a particular
          enquiry or activity, these references mean the relevant entity
          handling that matter. You can contact us at <a
            href="mailto:hello@exosquare.com">hello@exosquare.com</a
          > to identify that entity or ask about this policy.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="editorial-grid contact-section">
      <h2>Information we collect</h2><div class="prose">
        <p>
          When you contact us, we receive the information you choose to provide,
          such as your name, email address, organisation, role, message and
          attachments. This may include information about a proposed project,
          collaboration or employment enquiry. We collect this information
          directly from your correspondence and subsequent conversations.
        </p><p>
          Technical information, such as an IP address, browser type, requested
          pages and request times, may be processed by hosting and security
          services when they deliver and protect the website.
        </p><p>
          You can browse without creating an account. You may make a general
          enquiry without giving your name, although we need a way to respond
          and enough information to address your request. Please provide only
          information relevant to your enquiry and avoid sending sensitive
          information unless it is needed and an appropriate method has been
          agreed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="editorial-grid contact-section">
      <h2>How we use information</h2><div class="prose">
        <p>
          We use enquiry information to respond, assess proposals, arrange
          discussions and manage related correspondence or work. We may also use
          relevant information to maintain business records, protect our systems
          and rights, resolve disputes and meet legal obligations.
        </p><p>
          We use information for the purpose for which it was provided, related
          purposes you would reasonably expect, or another purpose permitted by
          applicable law. Where consent is required for a different use, we will
          seek it separately. Sending an enquiry does not subscribe you to a
          mailing list.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="editorial-grid contact-section">
      <h2>Sharing and overseas processing</h2><div class="prose">
        <p>
          Information may be accessed by people working on the relevant enquiry
          or activity and by service providers supporting it, including hosting,
          communications, IT support and professional advisory services.
          Disclosure is limited to what is reasonably needed for the relevant
          purpose. We may also disclose information where required or permitted
          by law, or where reasonably necessary to establish, exercise or defend
          legal rights.
        </p><p>
          Service providers may store or process information outside your
          country, including outside Hong Kong or Australia. Applicable privacy
          protections can differ between countries. Where we engage a provider
          to handle personal information, we require appropriate handling and
          protection through contractual or other reasonable safeguards, taking
          account of applicable law. Contact us if you need information about
          the arrangements relevant to your enquiry.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="editorial-grid contact-section">
      <h2>Retention and security</h2><div class="prose">
        <p>
          Enquiry records are held electronically in email and communications
          systems. We retain personal information for as long as reasonably
          necessary for the purpose for which it is held, taking account of the
          nature of the enquiry or relationship, legal recordkeeping
          requirements and the resolution of disputes. Information no longer
          needed is deleted or de-identified, subject to applicable retention
          requirements.
        </p><p>
          We take reasonable steps to protect personal information from misuse,
          loss and unauthorised access, alteration or disclosure. The measures
          appropriate to a record depend on its nature and how it is held. No
          online service or method of communication can guarantee absolute
          security.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="editorial-grid contact-section">
      <h2>Browser storage and external services</h2><div class="prose">
        <p>
          The website stores your light or dark appearance preference in your
          browser’s local storage. This preference is not sent to us by the
          website. You can change it using the theme control or remove it by
          clearing this site’s browser data. Without a saved choice, the website
          follows your device preference.
        </p><p>
          The website does not use analytics or advertising trackers, and its
          application code does not set cookies. It does not offer accounts,
          online purchases or newsletter signup. Fonts and the Nostr QR image
          are served locally with the site.
        </p><p>
          External links, including Nostr links and the QR destination, open
          separate websites or applications. Their own terms and privacy
          practices apply when you use them. Public Nostr activity may be
          distributed or copied by other participants and services. This website
          does not embed a Nostr feed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="editorial-grid contact-section">
      <h2>Access, correction and complaints</h2><div class="prose">
        <p>
          You can request access to or correction of personal information we
          hold about you, or raise a privacy concern, by emailing <a
            href="mailto:hello@exosquare.com">hello@exosquare.com</a
          >. Describe your request and the relevant interaction. We may need to
          verify your identity or ask for further details before providing
          access or making changes.
        </p><p>
          We will consider requests in accordance with applicable law. If a
          request cannot be met, we will explain the reason where permitted. For
          complaints, we will review the circumstances, seek any information
          needed to investigate and respond with the outcome and any proposed
          steps to address the concern.
        </p><p>
          You may also contact the relevant privacy regulator, including the <a
            href="https://www.pcpd.org.hk/"
            >Hong Kong Privacy Commissioner for Personal Data</a
          > or the <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/privacy/privacy-complaints"
            >Office of the Australian Information Commissioner</a
          >, where the matter falls within its jurisdiction.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="editorial-grid contact-section">
      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2><div class="prose">
        <p>
          We may update this policy to reflect changes in our activities, the
          website or applicable requirements. The date at the top identifies the
          latest version. Where a change requires further notice or consent
          under applicable law, we will provide that notice or seek that
          consent.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div></Base
>
